WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:09.107
Jack groaned when his alarm went off the next morning.

2
00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:16.099
"Yay!" Luke shouted from his own bed. "I get to watch swim practice today!"

3
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.420
"Great," Jack muttered sarcastically.

4
00:00:19.421 --> 00:00:28.178
His mother planned to stay at his practice today to make sure he didn't ditch it again. That meant Luke was staying too.

5
00:00:28.179 --> 00:00:33.098
Jack hauled himself out of bed. His back hurt.

6
00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:42.003
Yesterday, after his parents lectured him for approximately five million hours, they'd made him clean the kitchen and sweep and mop the floor.

7
00:00:42.004 --> 00:00:48.320
The only good thing about living in a small apartment was that it didn't take too long to clean it.

8
00:00:48.321 --> 00:00:52.134
Jack's parents had also made him email his coach.

9
00:00:52.134 --> 00:00:59.494
He apologized for quitting the team and politely asked—begged, really—for another chance.

10
00:00:59.495 --> 00:01:04.494
Hours later Coach Shin sent a short response: "See you tomorrow."

11
00:01:04.495 --> 00:01:14.432
As Jack put on his swimsuit and brushed his teeth, he wondered if Coach Shin would lecture him and give him chores too.

12
00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:19.558
He pictured himself scrubbing the deck of the pool while his teammates laughed at him.

13
00:01:19.559 --> 00:01:25.565
"I hate it here," he said to his reflection in the mirror. "Why did we ever move?"

14
00:01:25.566 --> 00:01:35.391
Jack went to the kitchen. His dad was standing by the stove, dressed for work in a button-down shirt and khaki pants.

15
00:01:35.392 --> 00:01:44.201
He lifted a ham-and-cheese omelet from a pan on the stove, slid it onto a plate, and passed it to Jack's mother.

16
00:01:44.202 --> 00:01:52.392
She put a buttery toasted bagel on the plate and handed it to Jack. "Enjoy," she said brightly.

17
00:01:52.393 --> 00:01:57.447
"Thank you. I'm really sorry about skipping practices," he said.

18
00:01:57.448 --> 00:02:05.876
"You apologized last night, and we've forgiven you," his mother said, sitting next to him at the small kitchen table.

19
00:02:05.877 --> 00:02:09.852
"I know it's hard to be the new guy in town," Jack's father said.

20
00:02:09.853 --> 00:02:17.779
"My first day of work here, I showed up in a business suit and tie. I was completely overdressed and completely embarrassed."

21
00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:26.771
"It's hard to be the new girl in town too. I miss my friends in Oklahoma and my book club and my walking group," Jack's mother said.

22
00:02:26.772 --> 00:02:30.255
"It's going to take time to get adjusted."

23
00:02:30.256 --> 00:02:39.328
Jack nodded. "I miss Noah and the other kids on the swim team. And, honestly, I miss being the best swimmer on the team.

24
00:02:39.329 --> 00:02:42.661
It seems like some of the kids here are really fast."

25
00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:47.820
"Competing with fast swimmers will help you improve your speed," Jack's father said.

26
00:02:47.821 --> 00:02:52.282
"But it's still hard," his mother said sympathetically.

27
00:02:52.283 --> 00:02:56.246
"Yeah," Jack said. "It's really hard."

28
00:02:56.247 --> 00:03:05.564
A few minutes later, Jack headed to the car with his mother and Luke. Laura was waiting there for them.

29
00:03:05.565 --> 00:03:08.401
Jack said hello but that was all.

30
00:03:08.402 --> 00:03:17.640
He spent most of the car ride staring silently out the window while Laura chatted politely with his mother.

31
00:03:17.641 --> 00:03:25.783
When they got to the community pool, Coach Shin nodded at him. "Hello, Jack," he said, his tone more stern than welcoming.

32
00:03:25.784 --> 00:03:29.687
"Thank you for letting me come back," Jack mumbled.

33
00:03:29.688 --> 00:03:35.220
One of his teammates sneered. "What are you doing here? I thought you quit the team."

34
00:03:35.221 --> 00:03:37.080
Jack didn't answer.

35
00:03:37.081 --> 00:03:43.536
The team did drills for the first 15 minutes of practice.

36
00:03:43.537 --> 00:03:52.020
Jack struggled hard but was able to keep up. And this time he didn't accidentally hum any Long-Hair Boys songs.

37
00:03:52.021 --> 00:03:57.758
"We've got only a few days before the meet. Let's make these practices count," Coach Shin said.

38
00:03:57.759 --> 00:04:04.089
"Last year the Pacific Piranhas beat us by two points. I don't want that to happen again.

39
00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:09.567
We'll start with the breaststroke today. Line up and swim across the pool and back.

40
00:04:09.568 --> 00:04:13.670
Pretend you're competing in the meet, and give it your best."

41
00:04:13.671 --> 00:04:21.669
Hulk was first in line. He practically flew across the pool.

42
00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:25.162
It wasn't just his huge size that made him fast.

43
00:04:25.163 --> 00:04:33.608
His streamline, a technique for swimming underwater, was perfectly straight, and he wasted no breaths and no motions.

44
00:04:33.609 --> 00:04:38.314
Watching him, Jack felt awed and envious.

45
00:04:38.315 --> 00:04:45.081
"He's incredible," Jack thought. "Definitely the best swimmer I've ever seen."

46
00:04:45.082 --> 00:04:54.710
When Jack's turn came, he swam as hard as he could and got a great time, close to his personal best.

47
00:04:54.711 --> 00:05:00.145
He knew he couldn't beat Hulk. But he thought he'd swum faster than most of the kids.

48
00:05:00.146 --> 00:05:10.720
As Jack emerged from the water, his brother clapped and shouted, "Yay, Jack! You're the bestest!"

49
00:05:10.721 --> 00:05:16.502
"Aww!" a girl said. "That little boy adores his big brother."

50
00:05:16.503 --> 00:05:20.118
"So sweet!" another girl said.

51
00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:28.197
Then Jack heard Laura's voice. "Luke is such a cutie," she said. "Luke and Jack look a lot alike."

52
00:05:28.198 --> 00:05:35.698
"Whoa!" Jack thought as he stared at Laura. "I think she just called me a cutie!" Jack grinned.

53
00:05:35.699 --> 00:05:39.592
Maybe it wasn't so bad having Luke come to his practices!

54
00:05:39.593 --> 00:05:42.406
"Come here, Jack," Coach Shin ordered.

55
00:05:42.406 --> 00:05:48.681
Uh-oh. Jack hunched his shoulders and walked over to the coach.

56
00:05:48.682 --> 00:05:55.457
Coach Shin put his hand on Jack's shoulder. "You swam the breaststroke much better today than last week.

57
00:05:55.458 --> 00:06:00.502
But you need to work on your form. You're not cupping your hands enough when they hit the water."

58
00:06:00.503 --> 00:06:07.081
"All right. Thank you," Jack said. Strangely, Mrs. Wilson had told him the same thing.

59
00:06:07.082 --> 00:06:10.264
Well, she'd actually shouted it at him.

60
00:06:10.265 --> 00:06:16.445
Jack returned to the water and tried following Coach Shin's advice—and Mrs. Wilson's.

61
00:06:16.446 --> 00:06:20.166
Cupping his hands more did seem to help a little.

62
00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:28.142
Jack and his teammates spent the next hour or so working on all the swim strokes.

63
00:06:28.143 --> 00:06:38.829
By the end of practice, Jack had done very well on the freestyle, okay on the backstroke, and pretty badly on the butterfly—but the "fly" stroke had always been hard for him.

64
00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:43.145
A few of the guys said, "Nice job" or "Not bad."

65
00:06:43.146 --> 00:06:52.187
At the end of practice, Jack approached Coach Shin. Nervously he cleared his throat.

66
00:06:52.188 --> 00:06:59.448
"Coach, I want to apologize again for skipping practices. Thank you for letting me come back."

67
00:06:59.449 --> 00:07:03.948
"Apology accepted and you're welcome. I'm glad you're back."

68
00:07:03.949 --> 00:07:11.785
The coach's tone wasn't exactly warm—more like lukewarm—but that was good enough for Jack.

69
00:07:11.786 --> 00:07:17.115
"It looks like your strengths are the breaststroke and the freestyle," Coach Shin said.

70
00:07:17.116 --> 00:07:21.612
Jack nodded. "I hope I can help our team beat the Pacific Piranhas."

71
00:07:21.613 --> 00:07:29.772
The coach shook his head. "I have a rule. Anyone who misses more than one practice isn't allowed to compete at the next meet."

72
00:07:29.773 --> 00:07:30.726
"But—"

73
00:07:30.727 --> 00:07:38.335
"That's my rule," Coach Shin said abruptly. "You follow it, or quit the team for real this time."

74
00:07:38.336 --> 00:07:53.432
Jack hung his head. "I understand," he mumbled. He did understand, sort of. But somehow it still felt incredibly unfair.

